From: Mayuka <mayuka.bulath@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:29:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Hen Pecks: sign in to keep stats across devices (Supabase)

Stats lived only in the browser, so a new phone or cleared storage lost
the streak. Players can now sign in with an email link (and Google, once
it's set up) and their stats are saved to an account.

- Finished games are now logged by day, and the stats are worked out from
  the log. Merging two devices unions the logs, so a day can never be
  counted twice. Totals from before this change become a one-time "base"
  that each device adds to the account once (tracked by a device id).
- supabase/schema.sql: pecks_players table with row-level security, and
  a pecks_sync function that merges and returns the player's row.
- Until CLOUD is filled in there's no sign-in button and nothing changes.
  Signing out keeps this device's own games.
- README: setup steps for the database, keys, redirects, email and Google.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
